{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0318e6798c363c9641107dd48e241fd62305b43e7c61e6e9182808db47b777ef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Feature flags include human_in_the_loop (tool approval prompts, default true) and mcp_enabled (default false), toggled via the [features] table in vtcode.toml."},{"claim_ids":["clm_162178fbb2ce931ce2e8e56772ac5136101131a67ab3b9465378587ac3b73c5c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Interactive sessions live-reload watched config changes with debouncing; safe settings apply without restart, and malformed edits keep the last valid configuration with a warning."},{"claim_ids":["clm_663bfe81efe3364e76cb4773e59ac35b9d050340db2ddc8ec8612fe76ca3cd33"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration uses vtcode.toml at workspace or platform config-directory layers, with environment-variable overrides and a legacy $VTCODE_HOME path kept as a migration source."},{"claim_ids":["clm_caa9a1ab5e14a82f06aaa03c7761877c88dbc28176966cac348494764dcc4a4a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent.provider setting supports many providers including openai, anthropic, google, deepseek, ollama, lmstudio, and others, with per-provider base_url and API-key environment variables configurable."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0318e6798c363c9641107dd48e241fd62305b43e7c61e6e9182808db47b777ef","clm_162178fbb2ce931ce2e8e56772ac5136101131a67ab3b9465378587ac3b73c5c","clm_663bfe81efe3364e76cb4773e59ac35b9d050340db2ddc8ec8612fe76ca3cd33","clm_caa9a1ab5e14a82f06aaa03c7761877c88dbc28176966cac348494764dcc4a4a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","id":"pg_20b8e42bc6555c499a707117d6dbf1c0","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vinhnx-vtcode-docs-config-config-md-18f7d26c76e2-7117d6dbf1c0.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_5774b46e756b59c487a8c1654de38cd9"],"title":"vinhnx/VTCode/docs/config/config.md @ 18f7d26c76e2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","id":"pg_2fdd5aaa569751c18002ee5c1cd5c6c0","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vinhnx-vtcode-docs-index-md-18f7d26c76e2-ee5c1cd5c6c0.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b48375c53ecf55bba1a14f5e287dce67"],"title":"vinhnx/VTCode/docs/INDEX.md @ 18f7d26c76e2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1e3bec124a4f73f70cdf323253c0b20a1b3e5515deefecf78676e391cf00e36a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Default public tool surface includes exec_command (shell via policy/sandbox/approvals), write_stdin for live-session continuation, and apply_patch with workspace-boundary checks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_48a6b59da80c47ab9878bd8c7835334964a4fd640576244c5919012c21f24dc0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ThreadEvent (vtcode-exec-events) is the authoritative runtime event contract feeding replay, checkpoints, memory, and trajectory export; follow-up inputs queue and inject one at a time at idle boundaries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_60046b34315663cfb147fe9d6b65a77b114c523287e08877ed52c61fda45c7d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Delegation is modeled as explicit thread spawning: child agents do bounded sidecar work, their output is advisory until the parent validates and merges it into the SessionMemoryEnvelope at turn boundaries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e5dbab108180acb00e3375600d1ea7b54fd606a3842be6720d12cccf0297428"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture separates the model (reasoning) from the harness (runtime supplying tools, context, sandboxing, state, and verification), organized as seven reinforcing subsystems."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6ef343e7928a4cf6ae926150393063eea497ee91f908e4d7e43fef9a518d0da1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI separates data on stdout from diagnostics on stderr, uses clap for argument parsing, isolates subcommands (ask, exec, chat) in dedicated modules, and handles SIGINT/SIGTERM gracefully."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7f3c0cc587b459a327597326855b28aedbc7c126ef8e0074808864109c192089"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A persisted SessionMemoryEnvelope summarizes objective, constraints, touched files, grounded facts, verification status, and delegated findings for resume and summarized-fork handoff."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a30db75e4cf6eaa56af6b0f0b2b3580641747e16e5690c7ce11bacaf859a410a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"With agent.harness.orchestration_mode = plan_build_evaluate, a planner writes spec/contract artifacts, the generator runs on the main session, and an evaluator performs a skeptical post-build pass; failed evaluation triggers bounded revision rounds."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1e3bec124a4f73f70cdf323253c0b20a1b3e5515deefecf78676e391cf00e36a","clm_48a6b59da80c47ab9878bd8c7835334964a4fd640576244c5919012c21f24dc0","clm_60046b34315663cfb147fe9d6b65a77b114c523287e08877ed52c61fda45c7d6","clm_6e5dbab108180acb00e3375600d1ea7b54fd606a3842be6720d12cccf0297428","clm_6ef343e7928a4cf6ae926150393063eea497ee91f908e4d7e43fef9a518d0da1","clm_7f3c0cc587b459a327597326855b28aedbc7c126ef8e0074808864109c192089","clm_a30db75e4cf6eaa56af6b0f0b2b3580641747e16e5690c7ce11bacaf859a410a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","id":"pg_32d0ac10b1965646a6976c7d94491f8a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vinhnx-vtcode-docs-architecture-md-18f7d26c76e2-6c7d94491f8a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"title":"vinhnx/VTCode/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md @ 18f7d26c76e2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","id":"pg_39dc75d3a50f5cbfba760edcc652a08b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vinhnx-vtcode-context-md-18f7d26c76e2-0edcc652a08b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9602389844c656088b8839c860a61877"],"title":"vinhnx/VTCode/CONTEXT.md @ 18f7d26c76e2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_16010ea108571dcb7a1d265fd945fe8ae46bc81d8f684e5b1dc761a0613afeb9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"VT Code is described as a secure, open-source terminal coding agent written in Rust, shipped as a single static binary for interactive and long-running autonomous work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_48a6b59da80c47ab9878bd8c7835334964a4fd640576244c5919012c21f24dc0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ThreadEvent (vtcode-exec-events) is the authoritative runtime event contract feeding replay, checkpoints, memory, and trajectory export; follow-up inputs queue and inject one at a time at idle boundaries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e5dbab108180acb00e3375600d1ea7b54fd606a3842be6720d12cccf0297428"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture separates the model (reasoning) from the harness (runtime supplying tools, context, sandboxing, state, and verification), organized as seven reinforcing subsystems."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8273e1126f3d9d7e38cf1b03c1ba2438054b74ed3c5244b458a991fc86deda54"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states the project is in active development and that local inference and some automation flows are experimental and may change between releases."}],"claim_ids":["clm_16010ea108571dcb7a1d265fd945fe8ae46bc81d8f684e5b1dc761a0613afeb9","clm_48a6b59da80c47ab9878bd8c7835334964a4fd640576244c5919012c21f24dc0","clm_6e5dbab108180acb00e3375600d1ea7b54fd606a3842be6720d12cccf0297428","clm_8273e1126f3d9d7e38cf1b03c1ba2438054b74ed3c5244b458a991fc86deda54"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","id":"pg_7529b0234bba5a9290e0127bf5f649bd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vinhnx-vtcode-readme-md-18f7d26c76e2-127bf5f649bd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8f7d27a517cb545db73607c1d4b75f5f"],"title":"vinhnx/VTCode/README.md @ 18f7d26c76e2","updated_at":"2026-09-